; COUNTRY.DEF - the countries in COUNTRY.SYS.  UTF-8.
;
; TOOLS\MKNLS.PS1 turns this into NLS\COUNTRY.ASM, which BUILD.CMD
; assembles into COUNTRY.SYS.  Run the script after changing a line.
;
; One line a country, sixteen fields:
;
;   code     what COUNTRY= takes: the international dialling code
;   name     for the reader only; no blanks in it
;   pages    the code pages the country has tables for.  THE FIRST IS
;            THE ONE "COUNTRY=code" WITH NO CODE PAGE GETS, so it is
;            the page of the video card's own font where that is sold:
;            437, or the national page where 437 lacks the alphabet
;   date     mdy, dmy or ymd, and what goes between the numbers
;   clock    12 or 24, and what goes between hours and minutes
;   number   the thousands separator and the decimal point
;            (sp = a blank)
;   list     what separates the items of a list
;   money    the currency symbol, four characters at most.  A second
;            spelling after a | is for a code page that lacks a
;            character of the first.  Then where it goes -
;              0  $1.00    1  1.00$    2  $ 1.00    3  1.00 $
;            - and how many digits follow the decimal point
;   yes no   the letters 21h/6523h takes for yes and for no
;   sort     which letters come after Z: - none, dk the Danish and
;            Norwegian three, sv the Swedish and Finnish three
;
;code name          pages        date  clock number list money   yes no sort
001 United-States   437,850      mdy - 12 :  ,  .  ,  $        0 2  Y N  -
002 Canada-French   863,850      ymd - 24 :  sp ,  ;  $        3 2  O N  -
003 Latin-America   437,850      dmy / 12 :  ,  .  ,  $        0 2  S N  -
